---
description: Canonical specification governance for the entire game repository
alwaysApply: true
---

The Git repository is the canonical source of truth.

Before making changes that affect systems, assets, UI, Blender exports, UE5 integration, or tool workflows:

1. Read `spec-manifest.yaml`.
2. Read `docs/governance/source-of-truth.md`.
3. Read `docs/governance/naming-and-versioning.md` before inventing Ids or asset filenames.
4. Read the relevant canonical system and asset specs.
5. Report missing, inaccessible, REVIEW, UNSET, or conflicting inputs.
6. Never treat chat history, model memory, or `.cursor/rules` as a replacement for canonical specs.
7. Do not change LOCKED facts without explicit user approval, a recorded diff, and a version update.
8. Candidate changes may be written as DRAFT/REVIEW, but must not overwrite LOCKED originals.
